---
import ToolDiscovery from "../../components/ToolDiscovery.astro";
import { guides } from "../../data/discovery.js";
import UtilityLayout from "../../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import ExtraUtilityApp from "../../components/ExtraUtilityApp.astro";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Ask a page or text"
  description="Ask a question. Explore a source-backed answer, supporting details and the context behind each point."
  seoDescription={guides["ask-a-webpage"].description}
  searchTitle={guides["ask-a-webpage"].title}
  slug="ask-a-webpage"
>
  <ExtraUtilityApp tool="qa" />
  <ToolDiscovery slug="ask-a-webpage" />
  <details class="prose tool-help">
    <summary>How answers and source coverage work</summary>
    <h2>Your source, organized around your question</h2>
    <p>
      Jev identifies relevant source material, distinguishes direct answers,
      explanations, procedures, comparisons and caveats, then selects an exact
      source sentence to introduce the answer. The application assembles the
      source’s own words into a readable result. It does not generate new prose
      or add outside facts. Open a citation to inspect where a point came from,
      or download the answer and its underlying source data.
    </p>
    <h2>Complete-source reading, honest limits</h2>
    <p>
      Pasted text may contain up to 2 MiB of UTF-8 text; questions may contain
      up to 1,000 characters. All source sections are processed rather than
      searching only the first 10,000 characters or 100 paragraphs. Large
      sources take longer, and processing every section does not guarantee that
      every relevant point was recognized. A failed section rejects the result
      instead of silently accepting a partial scan.
    </p>
    <p>
      Public HTTP/HTTPS pages and bare hostnames are supported. Reading is
      limited to 250,000 bytes, eight seconds and three redirects; every
      redirect repeats URL and public-address checks. The reader executes no
      page scripts or embedded requests. Logins, paywalls, access blocks,
      JavaScript-only pages and PDFs may require pasted text. These transport
      protections are separate from answer coverage and are not bypassed.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy and uncertainty</h2>
    <p>
      Only your explicit action sends source context and the question to Jev
      through the protected server. There is no account or input-history
      database. Source text and model judgments can be wrong; inspect the
      supporting material before relying on an answer.{" "}
      <a href="/privacy/">Privacy and operating limits.</a>
    </p>
  </details>
</UtilityLayout>
